WEBVTT

01:04.064 --> 01:05.982
WHEN LIFE GIVES YOU TANGERINES

01:10.487 --> 01:14.783
THE BLAZING SUMMER SUNSHINE

01:14.866 --> 01:16.576
It's so hot today.

01:17.077 --> 01:19.120
Wow, it's scorching hot.

01:19.954 --> 01:22.540
Perfect weather to torment
your daughter-in-law.

01:24.375 --> 01:27.087
They say 108 prostrations
should be enough.

01:29.172 --> 01:31.466
It would've worked already
if 108 were enough.

01:31.549 --> 01:32.884
She's wasted five years.

01:32.967 --> 01:35.136
Even Buddha's sick after 3,000.

01:38.098 --> 01:41.184
-Suffering yields dedication.
-You're just mean. Just mean.

01:41.267 --> 01:45.688
How can a lady of the house be so cruel
and expect more children from her?

01:46.356 --> 01:48.233
Let's be honest.
Not all children survive.

01:48.316 --> 01:50.443
You could have eight, and two might die.

01:50.527 --> 01:52.612
If the family she married into
valued sons, huh,

01:53.196 --> 01:54.322
she should be having plenty.

01:55.031 --> 01:56.908
How could she try to freeload
off our family?

01:56.991 --> 02:00.453
Her family didn't give us a single
silver spoon as dowry. Nothing at all.

02:00.537 --> 02:02.247
What about you?

02:02.914 --> 02:05.458
Did you bring us a silver spoon?
Is that why you had two?

02:08.128 --> 02:10.797
You can't stand me, but your
granddaughter-in-law is precious, huh?

02:12.841 --> 02:14.342
Let's go now, Ae-sun.

02:28.773 --> 02:32.235
If you make her do
3,000 prostrations,

02:32.318 --> 02:34.696
she'll be too exhausted to do housework.

02:34.779 --> 02:36.948
Yes, she does so much,
doesn't she?

02:38.032 --> 02:39.409
That'll be your pillow talk, huh?

02:39.492 --> 02:41.995
Go ahead, tell your husband
I made you do 3,000.

02:42.078 --> 02:44.455
He could take your side right away,

02:44.539 --> 02:47.458
but no husband likes
when his wife bad-mouths his mother.

02:47.542 --> 02:48.418
Huh?

02:48.501 --> 02:50.170
You know, the biggest mama's boys

02:50.253 --> 02:54.090
really want their wives to be
the most devoted daughters-in-law.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.384
So watch what you say, huh?

02:56.467 --> 02:59.220
Was that directed to my ears?

02:59.304 --> 03:00.680
Fine, I won't say anything.

03:00.763 --> 03:01.848
Sure you wouldn't.

03:02.515 --> 03:05.185
And, plus, he groans in pain each night.

03:05.268 --> 03:07.729
I don't wanna give him
more reasons to be upset.

03:07.812 --> 03:10.315
Well, good for you.

03:11.441 --> 03:12.650
They say a man

03:13.276 --> 03:16.738
stays with a wife he loves
despite despising her family.

03:17.488 --> 03:18.907
For me, it's the opposite.

03:18.990 --> 03:20.408
How dare you?

03:22.118 --> 03:23.661
Serves you right.

03:24.162 --> 03:27.457
Seems my granddaughter-in-law's
bested my daughter-in-law.

03:28.416 --> 03:31.336
Oh, she's so annoying.
Should I teach her a lesson?

03:32.003 --> 03:34.923
Hey, why did you just hit
the hareubang's nose?

03:35.006 --> 03:36.633
Huh? Hey.

03:37.425 --> 03:39.427
Why did you just hit his nose? Huh?

03:40.136 --> 03:41.763
Oh, uh, I'm sorry.

03:42.347 --> 03:43.473
Stop right there!

03:46.893 --> 03:48.937
YEOM SUN-NAM, YEOM SUN-BONG

03:49.020 --> 03:52.148
Even the government says
only having one child is patriotic.

03:52.815 --> 03:54.359
They keep saying sons though.

03:54.859 --> 03:56.819
Who cares if we birth sons anyhow?

03:57.654 --> 03:59.864
What was gained by raising Gwan-sik, huh?

04:00.365 --> 04:02.450
They did all that just to give him to me.

04:02.951 --> 04:05.495
Why did she keep throwing red beans at us?

04:07.038 --> 04:09.290
Who cares if my mom's spirit
is still here?

04:10.625 --> 04:14.087
So what if my mom wants to visit me?
So what?

05:15.606 --> 05:17.775
I can't even visit my mom's house now.

05:21.446 --> 05:22.780
Well, that's not right.

05:24.407 --> 05:26.534
I do miss her more now that I'm a mom.

05:29.078 --> 05:30.705
I miss my mom even more.

05:41.132 --> 05:42.925
Honestly, must be upsetting

05:43.009 --> 05:45.470
to not be permitted
to visit this house anymore.

05:48.473 --> 05:49.307
Mmm.

05:50.224 --> 05:51.142
Mmm.

05:53.519 --> 05:54.437
Mmm.

05:54.937 --> 05:56.230
Ooh! Oh.

06:02.195 --> 06:05.198
You can keep bringing her,
but we're not going to accept her.

06:05.281 --> 06:06.949
We're not taking in new people.

06:07.700 --> 06:09.744
She's so young.
Why do you always drag her here?

06:09.827 --> 06:12.789
Veteran haenyeo start their training
between six and seven.

06:12.872 --> 06:14.999
Who begins haenyeo work at the age of six?

06:15.083 --> 06:17.752
Children her age pick kelp
in the shallow waters.

06:17.835 --> 06:18.711
That's why.

06:18.795 --> 06:22.757
I heard that this spot's for beginners,
so you make her go play in the water now

06:22.840 --> 06:25.176
so she won't be so afraid of it later,
you know?

06:25.259 --> 06:26.886
-She your daughter?
-Mm.

06:27.845 --> 06:29.972
Oh, I don't even want to talk to you now.

06:30.056 --> 06:30.890
All right?

06:30.973 --> 06:34.435
And does Ae-sun know?
Did you ask if it's all right?

06:34.519 --> 06:36.270
Why do I have to get permission?

06:36.354 --> 06:37.563
She can't control me.

06:37.647 --> 06:40.650
Horses and people
must prove their worth to make a living.

06:41.401 --> 06:44.570
We want her to learn a skill.
Why would you be against her having that?

06:44.654 --> 06:45.863
Mak-cheon, listen to me.

06:46.823 --> 06:48.741
Every time we go back into the water,

06:48.825 --> 06:51.119
we ask God, "Don't let us die, Lord."

06:51.911 --> 06:54.414
That's why Gwang-rye
told Ae-sun every day,

06:54.497 --> 06:57.792
"Don't become a haenyeo.
Please don't bother learning to dive."

06:58.793 --> 07:00.711
If Gwang-rye didn't want
her daughter doing it,

07:00.795 --> 07:02.880
she wouldn't want
her granddaughter to do it.

07:02.964 --> 07:05.299
You responsible for keeping
Geum-myeong alive?

07:05.383 --> 07:06.551
Stop nagging and let her dive.

07:06.634 --> 07:09.262
You better mind your own business, ladies.
I'm done.

07:12.682 --> 07:13.891
Oh gosh.

07:15.935 --> 07:17.562
-Here.
-Oh my.

07:19.522 --> 07:21.149
Let's go. Let's go. Let's go.

07:21.232 --> 07:23.568
Let's go. My goodness.

07:25.570 --> 07:26.654
Well, damn it!

07:26.737 --> 07:28.698
I envy people with daughters!

07:29.907 --> 07:31.367
Wonder how many they'll have?

07:31.451 --> 07:35.037
Who's to blame when you're destined
to live as a housekeeper?

07:35.121 --> 07:37.290
They have two weeks left to pack,

07:37.373 --> 07:39.125
so why are you packing for them?

07:39.667 --> 07:41.169
Don't they have hands?

07:41.919 --> 07:45.381
How will you live now that those brats
won't be around anymore?

07:45.465 --> 07:47.091
Hey, they're not brats,

07:48.593 --> 07:49.719
and I get angry quick.

07:50.553 --> 07:52.513
-Also, my in-laws…
-Yes, yes.

07:53.306 --> 07:56.309
I know their influence reaches
the Jeju provincial office.

07:56.392 --> 08:00.521
You've told me countless times
that they have sway over lawmakers here.

08:01.105 --> 08:04.650
But does their influence extend
all the way to the mainland?

08:05.985 --> 08:07.528
I'm saying I stand with those kids.

08:08.112 --> 08:11.949
So don't be mean to Sun-nam and Sun-bong
and give them plenty of food to eat.

08:13.534 --> 08:15.495
What if I'm mean, then?

08:16.913 --> 08:20.208
I wanna be tough on them sometimes,
but it's pretty difficult.

08:20.917 --> 08:23.961
How can I when they call me "Mom, Mom"?

08:24.462 --> 08:28.090
After raising kids in your house
for ten years, they get to be yours,

08:28.799 --> 08:29.634
even if they're not.

08:30.551 --> 08:33.471
What matters more than blood is the heart.

08:35.640 --> 08:37.850
You still can't figure that out?

08:40.853 --> 08:41.687
Gimme.

08:53.783 --> 08:59.539
I'm… sure you have plenty
to be angry about with no one to talk to.

09:00.331 --> 09:01.165
Give me a call.

09:01.874 --> 09:03.209
Maybe you wanna trash-talk

09:03.709 --> 09:05.545
the hag that throws beans at you.

09:05.628 --> 09:06.754
I'll listen to you.

09:07.547 --> 09:11.092
You know
we're not friends like that, right?

09:27.650 --> 09:30.361
Honestly, I wasn't a mistress.

09:30.444 --> 09:31.862
I didn't steal him from her.

09:32.446 --> 09:34.991
We got married ten years
after she passed away.

09:35.074 --> 09:36.450
There's no need for enmity.

09:37.201 --> 09:39.036
You and I aren't meant
to be friends though.

09:39.120 --> 09:42.832
Oh, is that why you had to run away
with my yellow dress that night?

09:43.457 --> 09:45.585
I'm just not your friend.

09:50.006 --> 09:51.173
I do respect you.

09:56.554 --> 09:58.931
Now that I've lived in this household,

09:59.557 --> 10:01.017
I respect you.

10:01.100 --> 10:03.311
You're not destined to be a housekeeper.

10:03.394 --> 10:05.021
You just have the heart of one.

10:06.647 --> 10:07.523
So then,

10:08.482 --> 10:10.109
stick with your man.

10:11.402 --> 10:13.613
You said he's a good guy.

10:23.122 --> 10:24.415
Mm, then I…

10:26.792 --> 10:27.835
What?

10:28.336 --> 10:29.170
…guess…

10:30.129 --> 10:31.464
Um, I guess…

10:32.882 --> 10:34.592
What?

10:34.675 --> 10:37.386
-Spill it.
-I guess I can entrust them to you.

10:39.055 --> 10:40.139
My siblings.

10:41.515 --> 10:43.476
-Please let them…
-What?

10:43.559 --> 10:45.102
…finish school.

10:45.186 --> 10:46.979
Stop worrying about my children.

10:47.063 --> 10:47.980
Quit it.

10:49.857 --> 10:51.025
Yeah, but still,

10:51.609 --> 10:54.362
I wouldn't just get four popsicles
like you did back then.

10:54.445 --> 10:57.031
So if I get corn,
then I do get five, okay?

10:59.575 --> 11:03.287
I'm giving you this tricycle instead of

11:03.829 --> 11:05.247
popsicles.

11:06.082 --> 11:08.542
Just think of it as a moral

11:09.418 --> 11:12.797
school grant that I'm donating
to Geum-myeong, okay?

11:13.381 --> 11:17.259
Hand out a used tricycle
as a school grant. Really?

11:21.681 --> 11:24.892
After the time you sacrificed for this
family, you're only stealing the tricycle?

11:24.975 --> 11:27.269
What do you mean by "steal" exactly?

11:27.353 --> 11:28.896
You told me to take it.

11:32.441 --> 11:36.779
One well-raised daughter
is better than ten sons.

11:40.825 --> 11:43.202
Planned Parenthood Federation
of Korea.

11:50.209 --> 11:52.169
She took the corn again today.

11:52.253 --> 11:54.797
This time, I counted how many cobs we had.

11:55.589 --> 11:59.593
We have a thief in our own home
when we don't even have enough for us.

11:59.677 --> 12:01.762
It's not like she has parents to support,

12:01.846 --> 12:04.682
so why does she give
the little we have left

12:04.765 --> 12:07.601
to people who are barely family to her?

12:07.685 --> 12:08.894
There's tilefish inside.

12:10.312 --> 12:11.272
You brought tilefish?

12:11.856 --> 12:12.690
Tilefish

12:13.607 --> 12:14.608
for the corn cobs.

12:15.609 --> 12:17.611
Do you only care about your wife,
or what is it?

12:18.237 --> 12:22.575
Who's gonna take my side if my only boy
keeps on prioritizing his wife's side?

12:22.658 --> 12:24.285
Dad's supposed to be taking your side.

12:26.454 --> 12:27.663
What are you looking at?

12:28.164 --> 12:29.749
I can't look at my own husband?

12:29.832 --> 12:31.041
Uh, no.

12:31.959 --> 12:33.919
I should've raised some dogs instead.

12:36.005 --> 12:38.340
Hey, you stole the corn cobs
from the cauldron.

12:38.424 --> 12:40.509
Wow, Ae-sun, are you a refugee now?

12:40.593 --> 12:42.762
I gave them five corn cobs, you see?

12:43.262 --> 12:44.722
And brought all of these.

12:46.640 --> 12:48.476
Look at that.

12:57.777 --> 12:59.820
Oh, is this real?

13:09.497 --> 13:10.873
Why did you bring this one?

13:11.874 --> 13:13.292
Wearing this to go back to Busan?

13:13.876 --> 13:15.711
Throw red beans at them. Red beans.

13:15.795 --> 13:18.714
Some of the clothing
that they used to wear

13:18.798 --> 13:20.382
are very nearly new, really.

13:21.383 --> 13:24.845
You know, honestly, she could've given
the tricycle to her own baby,

13:24.929 --> 13:27.473
but instead,
she just gave it to Geum-myeong.

13:29.433 --> 13:33.437
Throw the tricycle away.
Girls shouldn't ride tricycles.

13:33.521 --> 13:37.525
If my husband were alive,
his pipe would've smacked you already.

13:37.608 --> 13:39.902
If a peddler shows up,
we'll barter the tricycle for taffy.

13:43.572 --> 13:46.158
Geum-myeong,
did you go play by the sea today?

13:46.242 --> 13:47.576
Geum-myeong, it's bedtime.

13:48.077 --> 13:50.120
Uh, going to bed already?

13:54.166 --> 13:55.584
She goes to sleep early.

14:00.172 --> 14:01.006
Good night.

14:01.715 --> 14:02.716
Good night.

14:02.800 --> 14:03.926
Sleep well.

14:04.468 --> 14:06.512
Hope you won't be as grouchy.

14:20.651 --> 14:24.989
COLLEGE ENTRANCE EXAM
PREPARATION WORKBOOK 1

14:37.877 --> 14:39.628
OH AE-SUN

14:44.466 --> 14:47.720
GENERAL EQUIVALENCY DIPLOMA
NAME: OH AE-SUN

15:04.612 --> 15:05.905
Where have you been?

15:10.075 --> 15:12.661
I just love red beans so much.

15:24.173 --> 15:25.007
You worn out?

15:26.675 --> 15:28.344
Should I just keep my trap shut?

15:28.427 --> 15:31.764
If you take my side,
it won't simply be hate.

15:31.847 --> 15:33.807
They will want to kill me as well.

15:33.891 --> 15:35.225
How can I help you?

15:42.858 --> 15:44.151
Let me try, huh?

15:45.152 --> 15:47.029
I'd rather be the bad guy
if you'll let me.

15:51.951 --> 15:52.952
The tricycle.

15:53.953 --> 15:56.830
Let Geum-myeong ride the tricycle.

15:56.914 --> 15:59.458
Geum-myeong has to be
able to ride it. Really.

16:02.002 --> 16:02.920
Really?

16:03.003 --> 16:04.463
If she can't even ride a tricycle,

16:04.546 --> 16:07.257
she'll just live in the kitchen
the rest of her days.

16:08.425 --> 16:11.345
I want Geum-myeong
to have everything, Gwan-sik.

16:11.428 --> 16:13.639
For her to have it all and do anything.

16:13.722 --> 16:15.849
I want… I want her to prosper in life.

16:16.600 --> 16:19.395
I don't want her to set the table forever.

16:19.478 --> 16:22.231
I want her to flip the table over instead.

16:25.859 --> 16:26.819
You flip it too.

16:27.403 --> 16:30.239
If you flip it,
I will clean the whole thing up.

16:34.493 --> 16:36.245
It's so frustrating.

16:38.998 --> 16:40.541
You can flip it or break it.

16:40.624 --> 16:44.003
You just tell me when,
and they'll take it out on me.

16:44.086 --> 16:46.213
Okay? I'll make sure
they know their limits.

16:46.296 --> 16:48.590
And, plus, they've been on me
for stealing fish to give you.

16:48.674 --> 16:50.676
-When?
-What?

16:51.343 --> 16:52.428
When, I said.

16:55.889 --> 16:57.182
I said when.

17:12.322 --> 17:14.491
Grant her a son.
Bless her womb.

17:14.575 --> 17:17.369
Please bless her womb with a boy.

17:17.453 --> 17:18.746
Grant her a son.

17:18.829 --> 17:20.706
Grant her a son, I beg you.

17:20.789 --> 17:22.332
Grant her a son.

17:22.416 --> 17:23.792
Bless her womb.

17:24.626 --> 17:25.711
Please.

17:25.794 --> 17:27.880
Bless her womb with a boy.

17:29.381 --> 17:31.091
Please grant her a boy.

17:32.176 --> 17:33.552
Grant her a son.

17:33.635 --> 17:35.304
Grant her a son, I beg you.

17:35.846 --> 17:36.764
Down.

17:36.847 --> 17:38.640
You better not tell Gwan-sik

17:38.724 --> 17:41.518
that I've been throwing red beans at you
first thing every morning.

17:42.019 --> 17:44.521
A talkative wife is no good anywhere.

17:48.817 --> 17:52.112
A woman who speaks a lot
and is lazy is useless.

17:53.822 --> 17:55.282
-Mm-hmm.
-Hmm.

17:57.659 --> 17:59.036
Ah no!

17:59.828 --> 18:02.581
How many times do I have to tell you
not to mix the peas like that?

18:03.082 --> 18:05.667
-Good God!
-She told him when.

18:05.751 --> 18:08.629
-Mom's morning started like any other day.
-Jeez.

18:11.215 --> 18:12.925
Though she was confined

18:14.134 --> 18:15.844
to a small treadwheel…

18:20.265 --> 18:23.102
she found
the small joys in life every day.

18:28.107 --> 18:29.399
It was 2,000 won.

18:29.483 --> 18:31.693
If you want 2,000 won
worth of taffy, do it.

18:35.364 --> 18:36.532
You're smiling?

18:37.699 --> 18:39.952
Peas, I want some peas, Mommy.

18:40.035 --> 18:42.663
Peas, oh, here.

18:43.831 --> 18:45.707
Peas. I want peas, please.

18:46.291 --> 18:48.043
Where are the peas?

18:48.127 --> 18:49.711
Where are they?

18:54.299 --> 18:55.425
Huh?

19:06.436 --> 19:09.148
-I wanna eat at this table from now on.
-Why?

19:11.775 --> 19:13.026
You insolent son.

19:14.278 --> 19:15.237
I'd like

19:16.321 --> 19:17.990
to eat with my mom at this table.

19:21.410 --> 19:22.911
Dogs are better. Dogs.

19:22.995 --> 19:25.455
Peas.
We bought some peas, Mommy.

19:27.958 --> 19:28.959
Be careful.

19:29.459 --> 19:31.545
Look, she's doing it. She's okay.

19:31.628 --> 19:33.797
CATCH A SPY
BRING HONOR TO THE FAMILY

19:33.881 --> 19:37.634
Grant me a grandbaby.
A grandson. Please send a grandson.

19:37.718 --> 19:39.928
Why not put her in a princess carriage?

19:40.596 --> 19:44.016
That tricycle's a waste of money.
You should've spent it on something else.

19:44.516 --> 19:45.851
I'm heading out.

19:45.934 --> 19:47.311
Be careful at sea.

19:49.980 --> 19:50.814
Babe.

20:03.452 --> 20:05.829
With a smile on her face,
as always,

20:06.330 --> 20:07.831
Ae-sun was spending

20:08.498 --> 20:10.876
all her twenties in the tiny kitchen.

20:13.962 --> 20:15.756
If she can't even
ride a tricycle,

20:15.839 --> 20:18.467
she'll just live in the kitchen
the rest of her days.

20:22.721 --> 20:25.641
I want Geum-myeong to have everything.

20:25.724 --> 20:27.601
For her to have it all and do anything.

20:28.185 --> 20:30.562
I want… I want her to prosper in life.

20:42.741 --> 20:44.034
Oh.

20:44.117 --> 20:45.327
Oh my.

20:48.455 --> 20:50.123
Hey, are you a centipede?

20:54.836 --> 20:58.090
Goodness!
You'd never get to wear all of these.

20:59.800 --> 21:02.970
When will she ever get
to wear all these shoes?

21:05.722 --> 21:07.432
Are you opening a shoe store?

21:08.350 --> 21:10.769
So then, I'd say,
just live with your mother.

21:12.020 --> 21:14.022
She said she likes her plants indoors.

21:26.159 --> 21:29.413
Your parents must've worked
so hard to send you to school

21:30.372 --> 21:32.124
with their limited means.

21:33.959 --> 21:37.421
They must be overjoyed
that you and Yeong-beom are dating.

21:37.504 --> 21:38.463
Yes.

21:39.673 --> 21:41.925
-They are excited.
-I'm sure they are.

21:43.760 --> 21:45.095
Of course they are.

21:46.847 --> 21:49.016
So you just got a job?

21:49.099 --> 21:50.517
Uh, uh, yes.

21:51.601 --> 21:52.853
The management

21:53.812 --> 21:56.356
says a lot of nice things about me.

21:56.857 --> 21:58.942
They say I'll be promoted really quickly.

21:59.526 --> 22:00.736
So you'll keep working?

22:01.236 --> 22:02.070
Huh?

22:02.154 --> 22:04.614
You want to keep working
after you get married?

22:04.698 --> 22:05.532
Uh…

22:06.283 --> 22:07.868
Yeong-beom and I…

22:07.951 --> 22:11.788
Um, he and I, we talked about it already.

22:11.872 --> 22:12.706
Listen,

22:13.707 --> 22:15.792
greed is a result of wanting approval.

22:16.293 --> 22:18.211
That desire turns to conceit.

22:18.295 --> 22:20.714
People who come into wealth quickly

22:21.423 --> 22:23.508
often feel the urge to show their riches.

22:24.009 --> 22:28.513
It's funny when women marry into wealth
and start dressing in luxury clothes.

22:31.391 --> 22:33.602
What? Have I offended you?

22:36.772 --> 22:38.106
Let me be frank now.

22:38.690 --> 22:41.026
Would you rather be promoted to manager

22:41.109 --> 22:43.362
or be the next
vice minister's daughter-in-law?

22:44.029 --> 22:47.366
Yeong-beom is our eldest son,
and he's very capable.

22:47.449 --> 22:49.159
So then why would his wife

22:49.242 --> 22:52.662
need a life outside the home
instead of supporting him?

22:53.163 --> 22:54.790
It frustrates you

22:55.415 --> 22:56.625
that I am old-fashioned?

22:59.169 --> 23:00.212
The thing is…

23:00.295 --> 23:04.174
I never want Geum-myeong
to feel inferior to anybody, anywhere.

23:08.428 --> 23:11.306
I'm as capable as Yeong-beom is, and I…

23:12.808 --> 23:14.976
I'm also my family's eldest child.

23:15.477 --> 23:17.979
I want to take care of my family
with my own money.

23:18.855 --> 23:19.689
And…

23:21.775 --> 23:23.318
…I have a strong drive,

23:23.944 --> 23:26.738
so just getting hired isn't enough.

23:26.822 --> 23:31.118
I want to be the manager, supervisor,
and even president. I want it all.

23:32.452 --> 23:36.206
That can't be a shameful ambition,
uh, isn't that true?

23:38.166 --> 23:39.501
You're right.

23:40.252 --> 23:43.964
I would think
that pretty girls would be more ladylike.

23:44.548 --> 23:46.299
They say indoor plants

23:46.383 --> 23:48.385
are a bit easier to manage.

23:54.224 --> 23:56.059
So what you mean is…

23:57.853 --> 24:00.063
is you're not an indoor plant either?

24:10.157 --> 24:11.366
What can I do?

24:12.159 --> 24:15.287
Apparently, I'm the not-pretty,
hard-to-handle eldest daughter.

24:17.372 --> 24:18.748
I've had enough, okay?

24:18.832 --> 24:20.500
I'm totally fine living without you,

24:20.584 --> 24:22.752
and I'm not desperate
to get married either.

24:42.105 --> 24:43.648
Good grief.

24:45.108 --> 24:48.195
You have more shoes
than I've ever worn in my life.

24:48.278 --> 24:51.114
Goodness, you make money to use like this?

24:51.615 --> 24:55.285
I didn't ask you to clean them.
It's so cold, and that's all you wanna do?

24:55.368 --> 24:56.870
They're all cheap shoes.

24:56.953 --> 24:58.872
They aren't worth your money.

24:58.955 --> 25:00.290
Goodness gracious.

25:04.544 --> 25:07.005
Why did you buy so many shoes, huh?

25:09.007 --> 25:10.842
This is all vanity

25:10.926 --> 25:13.470
and a… waste of money.

25:16.306 --> 25:18.642
Someone told me greed is conceit.

25:19.309 --> 25:20.227
What's that?

25:20.310 --> 25:22.229
Maybe because I grew up poor,

25:23.396 --> 25:24.981
I want to keep buying more.

25:31.071 --> 25:32.906
Maybe it's from deep pain.

25:35.075 --> 25:36.826
You made me beg,

25:37.869 --> 25:41.665
sometimes for three days, if I wanted
new clothes for field trips, you know.

25:42.165 --> 25:44.292
I wanted things, but we didn't have money.

25:44.876 --> 25:47.921
I grew up wanting stuff so bad,
and we couldn't ever get it.

25:49.297 --> 25:50.966
Now I never stop myself.

25:52.467 --> 25:54.177
It's very much cheap stuff.

25:54.803 --> 25:56.304
They're all impulse buys.

26:01.643 --> 26:03.645
It's not like I got what I liked

26:04.604 --> 26:06.648
refusing to buy you what you wanted.

26:07.148 --> 26:08.149
I still provided

26:08.233 --> 26:11.903
the best food and clothing
I could give you with what we had.

26:11.987 --> 26:15.073
What are you justifying right now?
You had me beg for things.

26:23.164 --> 26:24.874
Did something ha… happen today

26:25.500 --> 26:26.543
at the office?

26:27.043 --> 26:28.169
Damn it!

26:29.129 --> 26:30.380
Anyone giving you trouble?

26:30.463 --> 26:32.340
You wouldn't understand, would you?

26:32.424 --> 26:35.510
If you feel burned out,
then take time off.

26:35.594 --> 26:37.178
A break would be good.

26:37.262 --> 26:40.390
You work in an office building
and try to get a break.

26:40.473 --> 26:43.393
If it's so hard,
then quit and get married…

26:43.476 --> 26:44.311
And what?

26:44.394 --> 26:45.895
You want me to live like you?

26:45.979 --> 26:49.566
Get hitched into another poor family,
scraping by, spending my life…

26:53.069 --> 26:54.779
Breaking Mom's heart

26:55.780 --> 26:58.658
broke my own heart just the same.

27:00.285 --> 27:03.079
You're right. Yeah, you're right.

27:03.163 --> 27:04.664
Don't live my life over.

27:07.250 --> 27:08.501
But, you know…

27:11.880 --> 27:13.923
…I found happiness in my own way.

27:15.759 --> 27:18.094
There was sunshine in my life too.

27:19.929 --> 27:22.557
I've had so many picturesque moments.

27:29.105 --> 27:33.068
I'm asking you to recognize
that my life was worth living.

27:35.528 --> 27:36.363
Mm-hmm.

27:39.574 --> 27:41.242
It's an odd thing.

27:42.744 --> 27:44.579
Just give me the whole box. All of it.

27:44.663 --> 27:45.705
Oh, okay.

27:46.748 --> 27:50.168
Parents get upset about
what they can't do for their kids.

27:50.669 --> 27:54.005
Children get upset about
what their parents couldn't do for them.

27:56.675 --> 27:58.301
Ae-sun, pay your respects.

27:59.344 --> 28:00.178
Really?

28:00.762 --> 28:01.805
Mm.

28:01.888 --> 28:03.473
But I had no clue

28:04.182 --> 28:06.309
that my impoverished childhood…

28:06.810 --> 28:08.937
Her great-grandmother
may be a shaman,

28:09.020 --> 28:11.189
but she needs her mother's blessings.

28:11.272 --> 28:14.109
Nothing beats
a mother's dedication to her child.

28:14.192 --> 28:16.277
…my hunger-ridden youth

28:17.654 --> 28:20.907
was a fortress for which
they fought so fiercely.

28:21.616 --> 28:25.662
There is no better job in Jeju
than being a haenyeo.

28:26.705 --> 28:29.874
If we have one in the family,
she will then be our foundation.

28:29.958 --> 28:33.795
She won't need to ask us for a thing.
She'll make her own money,

28:34.421 --> 28:38.341
and as the eldest daughter,
she'll support the family.

28:49.811 --> 28:53.356
You can't expect a girl
to become a public official.

28:53.440 --> 28:55.900
She won't become a judge or an attorney.

28:56.818 --> 28:59.237
Becoming a haenyeo is her best option.

29:01.948 --> 29:04.075
-Oh!
-What?

29:04.159 --> 29:06.035
W… what have you done?

29:06.119 --> 29:09.122
-Oh, oh my. That… that girl… Oh, oh my.
-What in the…

29:09.205 --> 29:10.707
She's my daughter!

29:10.790 --> 29:13.209
She's not at the bottom
of the ladder in this house.

29:13.293 --> 29:14.335
She's my daughter!

29:15.545 --> 29:17.714
-How dare you!
-My daughter won't be a haenyeo.

29:18.423 --> 29:19.674
She'll never be one.

29:22.510 --> 29:25.221
Have you lost your mind?
Where are you taking her?

29:25.305 --> 29:26.556
Oh my.

29:26.639 --> 29:30.310
My mother developed a condition
because of her diving that killed her.

29:30.393 --> 29:32.562
Till the day she died,
she said, "Don't be a haenyeo."

29:32.645 --> 29:34.022
"Don't be a housekeeper."

29:34.981 --> 29:37.776
-Because… because I live as a housekeeper.
-How dare you!

29:38.818 --> 29:40.987
-Oh, Geum-myeong.
-A housekeeper, huh?

29:41.070 --> 29:43.990
You call serving your in-laws
and our ancestors housekeeping?

29:45.992 --> 29:48.828
You think I will let her
live like me as a housekeeper?

29:48.912 --> 29:52.415
-My daughter won't live my life here.
-You will be grateful for your life here.

29:52.499 --> 29:54.876
How dare you take a daughter
of the Yang family?

29:54.959 --> 29:56.419
She's my daughter. Mine!

29:56.503 --> 29:59.798
If you want a haenyeo in the family,
have your daughter do it. Why my daughter?

30:03.635 --> 30:04.969
Oh, she lost her mind.

30:05.053 --> 30:07.680
How dare you look me in the eye
and raise your voice at me!

30:07.764 --> 30:09.641
"If you want a haenyeo,
have your daughter do it"?

30:09.724 --> 30:12.602
Oh, god of the saints and god of the sea,

30:12.685 --> 30:15.647
watch over us. Watch over us.

30:17.398 --> 30:19.359
"Have your daughter do it"?

30:19.442 --> 30:22.946
How dare you utter such nonsense!
You must be out of your damn mind.

30:23.029 --> 30:24.656
I told you. I warned you.

30:24.739 --> 30:26.783
Her mother's soul is in her.

30:26.866 --> 30:29.118
Her spirit has possessed that girl.

30:29.202 --> 30:32.497
-And that's why she's lost her mind.
-You're right!

30:32.580 --> 30:36.167
That's what's happening.
Of course she acts just like her mother.

30:36.668 --> 30:40.755
You grew up in a worthless household,
raised by a lowly woman.

30:40.839 --> 30:42.423
This is an honorable household.

30:42.507 --> 30:44.133
Please watch over us.

30:44.217 --> 30:45.885
-Please watch…
-Hey, Gwan-sik.

30:46.427 --> 30:48.388
Did you see how she's been behaving?

30:48.888 --> 30:50.473
Did you see her demeanor?

30:51.057 --> 30:52.976
She says Geum-myeong isn't my grandchild

30:53.059 --> 30:56.896
and disrespected the ancestors and glared
and kept screaming at me and just…

30:56.980 --> 30:59.649
Say no more. Kick her out!

30:59.732 --> 31:03.194
The ancestors will not tolerate her!

31:03.278 --> 31:05.280
Grandma, have you been
throwing beans at her?

31:06.197 --> 31:09.534
Kick her out of here!
Kick her out! Kick her out! Kick her out!

31:10.285 --> 31:12.579
I hadn't hit her ever before.

31:12.662 --> 31:14.998
Oh dear.
This is just too much.

31:15.498 --> 31:16.583
I can't breathe now.

31:18.126 --> 31:19.085
-Oh no.
-Oh!

31:19.168 --> 31:21.838
Oh no. Oh no. Mom!
Ae-sun, you're giving her a heart attack.

31:21.921 --> 31:23.298
Oh my. Oh my.

31:23.381 --> 31:25.091
Mom. Grandma.

31:25.174 --> 31:28.344
I'm the reason Ae-sun came here.
Not to be your daughter-in-law.

31:29.679 --> 31:31.055
-What?
-You won't see…

31:32.265 --> 31:33.516
You won't see Ae-sun anymore.

31:34.767 --> 31:36.769
I won't let her live here.

31:41.566 --> 31:43.443
How dare she!

31:43.526 --> 31:45.236
Kick her out!

31:45.320 --> 31:46.863
Kick her out!

31:46.946 --> 31:48.865
Oh my!

31:54.037 --> 31:55.455
Why don't you wear them?

31:56.247 --> 31:58.124
They suit you better, I think.

32:00.710 --> 32:02.629
They fit really well, yes.

32:05.298 --> 32:08.301
Jeez, um,
you should've married a rich guy.

32:08.384 --> 32:11.387
Then you could be all dressed up
in floral patterns all the time.

32:12.555 --> 32:14.182
You do have some regrets, right?

32:16.476 --> 32:20.730
If you told me to, uh,
go back and marry your dad again, I'd say…

32:20.813 --> 32:21.856
Of course, you wouldn't.

32:23.566 --> 32:24.692
Yeah.

32:26.945 --> 32:27.820
I'd do it.

32:29.530 --> 32:31.074
-Geum-myeong.
-Oh.

32:31.991 --> 32:33.076
What's this?

32:33.159 --> 32:34.160
Hey there.

32:34.243 --> 32:37.205
Oh, I told you
not to buy two bags.

32:37.288 --> 32:38.498
Didn't I say that?

32:38.998 --> 32:41.334
She can buy her own peas, you know?

32:41.417 --> 32:42.418
What did you pay?

32:42.502 --> 32:45.463
-You get scammed again?
-Look, I brought a whistle.

32:45.546 --> 32:47.131
Oh, it's so loud!

32:47.215 --> 32:49.342
-World's scary.
-Look, babe. My shoes.

32:49.425 --> 32:51.386
-Aren't they cute?
-Oh, they look good.

32:52.387 --> 32:53.763
-Yeah.
-They fit great.

32:53.846 --> 32:54.681
They look perfect.

32:54.764 --> 32:58.226
DODONG-RI VARIETY SHOP

32:58.309 --> 33:00.812
ONE ROOM, ONE KITCHEN
MONTHLY RENT, NO DEPOSIT NEEDED

33:21.749 --> 33:24.127
GA, NA, DA, RA…

33:28.965 --> 33:32.093
-Geum-myeong, you want some peas?
-I want some peas.

33:32.176 --> 33:36.347
One more time. Here are some peas.

33:36.431 --> 33:39.183
-Here are some peas.
-Good. Eat some more.

33:40.059 --> 33:42.020
One more time. You want some peas?

33:42.103 --> 33:44.063
-I want some peas.
-Yes!

33:44.147 --> 33:45.523
My darling.

33:45.606 --> 33:49.068
-Squid. Squid.
-Squid? You want some squid?

33:49.610 --> 33:50.778
Squid.

33:53.614 --> 33:56.743
Squid, squid. Oh.

33:56.826 --> 33:59.370
-That's a good girl.
-Is it good? Is it good?

34:01.414 --> 34:03.207
Landlord. Landlord.

34:12.759 --> 34:15.136
Hey, not those. Auntie gave them to us.

34:15.219 --> 34:18.389
Won't he ask why we've got
abalone to eat when we can't pay rent?

34:23.394 --> 34:24.353
Yes, sir!

34:26.397 --> 34:27.565
Oh.

34:27.648 --> 34:29.942
Sir, I, uh,

34:30.026 --> 34:32.653
I am looking for
a new fishing job right now.

34:33.988 --> 34:38.117
Could we pay rent
at the very end of the month?

34:38.201 --> 34:40.244
Just pay me in the fall if that's better!

34:40.328 --> 34:43.706
No, that's not it. I'm not implying
we're trying to scam you, okay?

34:43.790 --> 34:45.166
Sir, hello.

34:45.249 --> 34:47.502
I'll watch the store
more often if you like.

34:47.585 --> 34:50.713
Someone came during the day
and handed me your rent for three months.

34:50.797 --> 34:52.256
And you… you weren't aware of that?

34:53.007 --> 34:55.093
Huh? Who did?

34:55.176 --> 34:57.678
Someone handed you three months of rent?

34:57.762 --> 35:00.807
Is there anyone named Do in your family?

35:02.016 --> 35:04.393
Do you have a relative named Do?

35:04.477 --> 35:06.395
Someone from the Do family paid for it.

35:06.479 --> 35:08.856
So if you pay the rent on time,

35:09.482 --> 35:11.234
I'll give you pork.

35:17.573 --> 35:20.243
DO HUI-JEONG SCHOLARSHIP
AMOUNT: 10,000 WON

35:30.795 --> 35:32.255
Stop glaring at me.

35:33.047 --> 35:33.965
Who is she?

35:35.133 --> 35:36.467
Who's Hui-jeong?

35:37.093 --> 35:39.929
What? I've been side by side
with you since you were ten.

35:40.429 --> 35:41.472
Really? Hui-jeong?

35:42.640 --> 35:45.977
Mm, yeah. Nobody ever had a thing for you.

35:46.978 --> 35:49.188
Tell me how you're so sure.

35:49.272 --> 35:51.774
I've never known anyone
from the Do family.

35:54.068 --> 35:55.278
What about your grandma?

35:55.987 --> 35:58.322
My grandmother's name is Kim Chun-ok.

35:58.406 --> 36:00.241
My aunt's name is Hyeon Yi-suk.

36:00.741 --> 36:03.244
Most importantly,
my grandmother is really poor.

36:04.579 --> 36:06.706
My grandma is Park Mak-cheon.

36:06.789 --> 36:08.249
My mom is Kwon Gye-ok.

36:09.750 --> 36:11.002
It could be Mom.

36:11.502 --> 36:15.381
Maybe my mom went into
the body of a rich housewife,

36:15.464 --> 36:18.342
and she had her dip into her account
at the bank and then…

36:47.413 --> 36:50.291
Oh, come on.

36:50.374 --> 36:51.584
Oh, come on!

36:54.003 --> 36:56.631
Why are they so inconsiderate?
How dare they!

36:57.506 --> 36:59.091
Your landlady said

36:59.175 --> 37:01.510
you guys get busy
as soon as it's 9:00 p.m.

37:02.428 --> 37:06.641
At your age, yeah, I guess
you would be diligent in that, huh?

37:06.724 --> 37:09.727
If you're so diligent about
turning off the lights at night,

37:09.810 --> 37:12.355
of course
the goddess of fertility would bless you.

37:12.438 --> 37:15.816
Look how happy she is
since leaving the in-laws.

37:15.900 --> 37:19.070
Hmm? Living without stress
helps with pregnancy too.

37:19.153 --> 37:22.281
If her in-laws tormented her
all day, and he walked into their room,

37:22.907 --> 37:26.202
she wouldn't want to make love
to her mother-in-law's son.

37:26.285 --> 37:28.454
Oh, of course
she wouldn't want to

37:29.413 --> 37:31.165
make love to him then.

37:31.249 --> 37:35.294
They're diligent, sure,
but the one I'm most proud of is…

37:36.462 --> 37:39.382
…Geum-myeong.
Oh, yes. What a gift you are.

37:40.007 --> 37:41.509
Living in that tiny room.

37:41.592 --> 37:43.302
My goodness gracious.

37:43.803 --> 37:46.430
As long as they want them,

37:47.056 --> 37:49.308
then a one-bedroom house
can support six kids, I think.

37:49.392 --> 37:51.852
Oh my. Oh my.

37:52.353 --> 37:54.355
She's turning into Gwang-rye already.

37:54.438 --> 37:58.067
This bookworm of a girl
is now a middle-aged woman. Jeez.

37:58.150 --> 38:01.320
If you lived closer, we'd see you
as much as we used to see Gwang-rye.

38:01.404 --> 38:04.615
You came all the way back here
just because your rent is a lot less?

38:04.699 --> 38:05.700
Leave her alone.

38:05.783 --> 38:08.911
If she lived here, her mother-in-law
would be over here all the time.

38:08.995 --> 38:11.956
It's easier to make money
if you know folks.

38:12.039 --> 38:14.625
Newbies aren't liked by islanders.

38:16.919 --> 38:19.213
Hey, how's Gwan-sik's fishing job?

38:20.131 --> 38:22.466
Well, he's hard-working,
as you know.

38:23.676 --> 38:26.512
He hasn't told you
what it is he does, has he?

38:26.595 --> 38:30.224
-You, you, you, you, watch your mouth.
-She needs to know though.

38:30.725 --> 38:32.643
Why? What is it?

38:34.312 --> 38:37.023
Gwan-sik hasn't said for whom he works?

38:38.316 --> 38:41.610
Hey, is your hand okay?

38:45.114 --> 38:46.073
-Oh!
-Oh no!

38:51.579 --> 38:52.413
What's this?

38:53.539 --> 38:55.666
-What happened to your hand?
-It's fine.

38:57.626 --> 38:59.670
You should've come
as soon as you got hurt.

38:59.754 --> 39:02.590
If you wait too long,
your fingers won't heal right.

39:05.634 --> 39:07.219
Big dummy. You said nothing.

39:07.303 --> 39:10.222
If you were hurt, you should've asked them
to turn back to shore.

39:10.306 --> 39:14.060
What's so glorious about fishing that
you'd pull the net and break your fingers?

39:17.938 --> 39:19.357
Cat got your tongue or what?

39:22.568 --> 39:24.403
Life itself isn't evil,

39:24.904 --> 39:25.988
but money is.

39:26.781 --> 39:30.242
Unfortunately, that family has control
over the seas on this side of the island.

39:30.326 --> 39:32.828
You can't get fishing work in Dodong-ri

39:33.329 --> 39:35.289
and not work for that guy.

39:35.373 --> 39:37.208
That's why he works for that guy.

39:37.833 --> 39:38.834
You don't know.

39:38.918 --> 39:42.546
He's young, but he's trying to be
the head of his household.

40:25.297 --> 40:26.215
Hey, babe.

40:30.803 --> 40:31.720
Honey!

40:33.639 --> 40:36.517
Hey, can you not hear me?

40:36.600 --> 40:38.352
Hey, help me get this inside.

40:40.688 --> 40:41.689
Oh man.

40:42.815 --> 40:44.400
Asleep without dinner again.

40:53.159 --> 40:54.952
Here you go. Right there.

40:56.203 --> 40:58.622
Dad's a baby. He sleeps all day like one.

41:00.124 --> 41:01.208
Sweetie.

41:03.085 --> 41:04.253
Oh my.

41:05.171 --> 41:06.046
It's hot.

41:07.506 --> 41:09.049
You should change, right?

41:13.095 --> 41:13.929
Oh.

41:15.264 --> 41:17.057
You keep wearing long sleeves.

42:35.010 --> 42:37.096
Do you need to be on that squid boat?

42:38.097 --> 42:40.516
You know, a man needs his rest.

42:40.599 --> 42:43.018
Dad, bring us a hundred squids, okay?

42:43.102 --> 42:45.813
Dad doesn't need to bring any squids back.

42:47.940 --> 42:48.774
I will

42:49.275 --> 42:50.901
bring so many squids for you.

43:07.793 --> 43:08.919
Hey, babe!

43:14.925 --> 43:16.510
Catch a lot of fish!

43:17.011 --> 43:19.221
Catch so many squids for me!

43:32.151 --> 43:33.569
-Go.
-Go.

44:00.471 --> 44:01.847
It looks yummy.

44:05.601 --> 44:06.727
CREAMER - INSTANT COFFEE

44:13.734 --> 44:15.736
You only get up to four for free.

44:20.324 --> 44:23.077
I think I'll get another can of sugar.

44:24.244 --> 44:26.288
-How dare you!
-How dare you!

44:26.372 --> 44:27.539
Die!

44:27.623 --> 44:29.708
-Why would I die?
-How dare you!

44:29.792 --> 44:32.044
-Ah!
-How dare you! How dare you!

44:32.127 --> 44:34.129
You dare challenge your older brother?

44:34.672 --> 44:36.882
How dare you! How dare you!

44:36.965 --> 44:38.884
-You really want to fight me?
-Ah-ha!

44:38.967 --> 44:42.513
I… I didn't get to bring you kimchi

44:42.596 --> 44:44.515
or visit when you were moving,

44:45.015 --> 44:46.892
so I wanted to say hi today.

44:49.103 --> 44:52.481
How are his fingers doing?
Are they healing all right, Ae-sun?

44:53.440 --> 44:56.985
He's……getting acupuncture.

44:57.569 --> 44:58.404
Ah.

44:58.487 --> 45:00.322
I nagged at my husband a little.

45:00.948 --> 45:03.283
If a man was hurt,
he should've turned the boat around.

45:03.367 --> 45:05.536
As if squids
are more important than people.

45:06.412 --> 45:09.540
Mr. Kim and Mr. Park
asked him to turn the boat around.

45:09.623 --> 45:11.709
They happened to have full nets that day.

45:12.209 --> 45:15.129
I understand why
my husband got a bit greedy.

45:18.465 --> 45:20.592
Mr. Yang is something else though,
isn't he?

45:20.676 --> 45:23.554
How did he stay on that boat
overnight with those fingers?

45:24.346 --> 45:27.641
If it were me, I would've been
rolling on the floor in pain.

45:28.559 --> 45:32.187
So the captain
didn't turn the boat around?

45:33.272 --> 45:34.273
Sorry?

45:34.773 --> 45:36.650
He didn't turn the boat around?

45:37.192 --> 45:38.026
Oh…

45:39.445 --> 45:42.614
My husband can't open his hand fully now.

45:46.326 --> 45:48.203
He moans in pain each night too.

45:48.746 --> 45:50.372
You don't need to worry about that.

45:50.456 --> 45:54.042
I did ask again and again
for my husband to quit hitting Mr. Yang,

45:54.126 --> 45:57.171
so he, uh, he says he's really stopped
beating him up.

45:58.464 --> 46:01.300
I don't know why
he's particularly mean to Mr. Yang.

46:04.219 --> 46:08.557
My husband does have a temper,
but he's not a bad guy, you know.

46:08.640 --> 46:09.558
How dare you!

46:11.769 --> 46:14.188
You wanna mess with me?
I'll knock some sense into you!

46:14.271 --> 46:15.606
How dare you!

46:15.689 --> 46:18.650
How dare you! How dare you! Damn it!

46:18.734 --> 46:19.860
How dare you!

46:19.943 --> 46:20.986
How dare you!

46:21.487 --> 46:22.404
How dare you!

46:24.031 --> 46:25.157
How dare you!

46:26.700 --> 46:28.243
You wanna mess with me, huh?

46:29.286 --> 46:30.871
You always leave so early.

46:31.371 --> 46:32.998
You're a big deal?

46:33.081 --> 46:35.375
That man can't ever wait to go home.

46:36.835 --> 46:40.005
You always bring packed lunches.
What's packed in that bag, huh?

46:40.839 --> 46:42.049
Goodbye.

46:42.132 --> 46:43.342
Hey, asshole!

46:49.056 --> 46:51.892
-You're driving the boat.
-Oh, come on, Captain.

46:51.975 --> 46:55.979
Do you have a crush on Gwan-sik?
Why hold back a man who wants to go home?

46:56.063 --> 47:00.359
I'm gonna drink a box of booze,
so just stand by and drive this damn boat.

47:00.442 --> 47:03.070
But, uh, Captain, he lives so close by.

47:03.153 --> 47:04.571
Hey, man, listen!

47:05.113 --> 47:09.368
If the captain doesn't get off the boat,
then no one gets off the boat either.

47:09.451 --> 47:12.621
Supporting the captain is also
an element of working here, okay?

47:12.704 --> 47:13.622
Get it?

47:14.581 --> 47:15.415
Know what I'm saying?

47:17.292 --> 47:19.878
Okay, let's get to work.

47:20.879 --> 47:22.047
Let's get to work.

47:22.548 --> 47:23.465
Now.

47:27.177 --> 47:28.136
Don't feel like it?

47:30.639 --> 47:31.974
Wanna mess with me?

47:32.057 --> 47:34.059
Tell me if you're not pleased
about what I said.

47:34.142 --> 47:36.520
Please speak up
and buy your own boat, kid.

47:37.896 --> 47:41.191
Oh, really? So what was it you said again?

47:41.275 --> 47:42.150
"Shut up, man"?

47:50.534 --> 47:53.954
Ms. Park, don't justify
everything he does.

47:55.789 --> 47:57.416
Yes, life is tough.

47:58.542 --> 47:59.543
Still, I think

48:00.294 --> 48:02.170
what isn't right isn't right.

48:03.338 --> 48:05.841
Look, if you don't want to,
just say so.

48:06.466 --> 48:08.010
You a mute or what, Gwan-sik?

48:08.635 --> 48:11.638
Oh. Because you don't have a boat, right?

48:11.722 --> 48:14.057
All right. All right, all right, I see.

48:19.855 --> 48:21.773
No, I don't want to.

48:22.357 --> 48:23.191
What?

48:23.275 --> 48:25.235
I can't lie about wanting to.

48:28.739 --> 48:29.573
Hey!

48:32.826 --> 48:33.785
Excuse me.

48:36.872 --> 48:37.789
Oh.

48:48.592 --> 48:51.178
Just can't wait to get home, huh?

48:54.473 --> 48:55.933
Why are you taking my squids?

48:56.808 --> 48:59.728
You can't be taking these
except if I let you. Get that?

49:00.729 --> 49:02.022
What boat do you own?

49:02.689 --> 49:05.359
You can have these if I let you.
You can stay back if I say so.

49:05.442 --> 49:09.154
Why are you always leaving early? Why?
What, do you like your wife that much?

49:09.237 --> 49:13.075
What's there to like? What?
Say something. Why don't you tell me?

49:13.158 --> 49:15.243
Are you crazy for her?

49:15.327 --> 49:17.871
You passionate every night, huh?

49:18.622 --> 49:20.582
Are you just dying to see her, are you?

49:21.375 --> 49:22.209
Yes.

49:22.834 --> 49:24.086
I'm dying to see her.

49:25.879 --> 49:26.713
What?

49:29.591 --> 49:32.052
You bunch of losers.
Gosh, you are such a punk.

49:32.552 --> 49:35.055
Seriously, man. Really?
What? You don't know?

49:35.681 --> 49:37.724
How dare you! How dare you, kid!

49:37.808 --> 49:40.185
And why don't you ever
wanna go home, Captain?

49:40.894 --> 49:42.312
-What'd you say?
-What?

49:43.355 --> 49:44.606
Do you feel lonely there?

49:45.649 --> 49:47.567
Because she doesn't treat you
the way you like?

49:49.820 --> 49:51.446
Oh jeez.

49:55.951 --> 49:58.036
Oh shit.

50:02.290 --> 50:03.583
That asshole.

50:10.507 --> 50:13.010
You punks need me
to beat some sense into you?

50:13.593 --> 50:14.636
Do you?

50:14.720 --> 50:19.975
You asshole!

50:20.058 --> 50:23.895
Asshole!

50:23.979 --> 50:25.772
Asshole!

50:35.615 --> 50:40.537
Hey, you asshole!

50:40.620 --> 50:44.332
You asshole!

50:45.208 --> 50:48.211
Dad always said
Mom wasn't really like a rose

50:49.296 --> 50:50.589
but more like a whistle.

51:01.975 --> 51:04.519
Gwan-sik won't work… for you

51:05.353 --> 51:06.188
ever again.

51:07.773 --> 51:09.107
He's done working for you!

51:12.736 --> 51:15.947
'Kay, don't do it.
Go away, man, just go home.

51:16.031 --> 51:18.075
My brother's the chief
of the fishing village.

51:18.158 --> 51:20.869
Don't think about getting
on a boat in Dodong-ri again!

51:21.703 --> 51:23.955
Boy, I dodged a bullet on that one.
Asshole!

51:24.039 --> 51:25.540
That girl, how dare she!

51:25.624 --> 51:27.292
The little brat! Reckless.

51:27.375 --> 51:30.420
The husband and the wife are equally bad.

51:37.094 --> 51:38.637
Take this!

51:39.346 --> 51:42.140
You need me to beat some sense into you?

51:43.225 --> 51:44.434
Why you little…

51:44.518 --> 51:45.644
How dare you!

51:45.727 --> 51:46.561
Huh?

51:47.187 --> 51:49.856
You should come to your senses first,
and then we'll see…

51:49.940 --> 51:50.941
we'll see…

51:51.024 --> 51:53.443
we'll see who really dodged a bullet here…

51:53.527 --> 51:54.569
How dare you!

51:57.155 --> 51:58.073
You wench!

51:59.116 --> 52:01.034
Ouch!

52:03.328 --> 52:05.622
Sang-gil's nickname needs a change.

52:05.705 --> 52:07.082
Dodong-ri's asshole.

52:07.874 --> 52:10.001
Yeah, "Asshole!"

52:12.671 --> 52:15.173
Oh man. Oh, that hurts so much.

52:21.429 --> 52:23.181
A whistle. A whistle.

52:24.099 --> 52:25.267
You're a human whistle.

52:29.771 --> 52:31.565
You kicked him. Why are you crying?

52:53.128 --> 52:56.006
We don't need
a water heater. It doesn't use coal.

52:57.299 --> 52:58.842
What about the draft?

53:00.635 --> 53:02.262
You said if you could do it,

53:03.346 --> 53:05.473
you'd do it all over,
and you'd marry me again.

53:07.267 --> 53:08.602
Mom always said…

53:09.728 --> 53:12.272
-Would you?
-Why would I?

53:12.898 --> 53:13.899
I'm fed up with you.

53:14.941 --> 53:18.361
…out of all of us,
Dad's the one who pains her the most.

53:18.445 --> 53:20.447
Steel wears out too, doesn't it?

53:20.530 --> 53:22.407
Why is your body already breaking down?

53:22.490 --> 53:24.034
Stop scaring me, okay?

53:25.493 --> 53:26.703
Oh my.

53:31.374 --> 53:33.793
You've been lifting big loads
since you were ten.

53:33.877 --> 53:35.754
Of course you're having issues.

53:36.630 --> 53:39.341
Don't worry, Ae-sun.
I'm going to outlive you anyway.

53:40.217 --> 53:43.178
What? When I die,
would you want another wife?

53:51.686 --> 53:53.021
Would you like a new wife?

53:53.939 --> 53:55.523
I couldn't treat you like that.

53:56.650 --> 53:58.568
I don't want someone to replace you.

53:59.319 --> 54:01.196
I'd feel better sending you off first

54:02.072 --> 54:03.448
and then following after.

56:55.286 --> 56:59.791
"THE SAME SKY, THE SAME STARS,
ETCHED IN THE SAME HEARTS."
